{"id":"apex_canvas_ApplicationContext_getCanvasUrl","title":"getCanvasUrl()","content":"<a name=\"apex_canvas_ApplicationContext_getCanvasUrl\"><!-- --></a><h1 class=\"helpHead1\">getCanvasUrl()</h1><div class=\"body refbody\">\n<div class=\"shortdesc\"><span class=\"ph\" id=\"shortdesc\"><a name=\"shortdesc\"><!-- --></a>Retrieves the fully qualified URL of\nthe canvas app.</span></div>\n\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2 class=\"helpHead2\">Signature</h2>\n<p class=\"p\"><samp class=\"codeph apex_code\"><span class=\"keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"keyword\">String</span> getCanvasUrl()</samp></p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2 class=\"helpHead2\">Return Value</h2>\n<p class=\"p\">Type: <a class=\"xref\" href=\"atlas.en-us.apexref.meta/apexref/apex_methods_system_string.htm#apex_methods_system_string\" title=\"Contains methods for the String primitive data type.\">String</a></p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2 class=\"helpHead2\">Usage</h2>\n<p class=\"p\">Use this method to get the\nURL of the canvas app, for example: <span class=\"ph filepath\">http://instance.salesforce.com:8080/canvas_app_path/canvas_app.jsp</span>.</p>\n</div>\n\n</div><div id=\"sfdc:seealso\" class=\"related-links\"></div>"}